Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:53:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add World Markers plugin (worldmarkers.dll) with a module API

New plugin Plugins/WorldMarkers.lua lets boss modules place ground
markers through WeirdUtils' worldmarkers.dll:

  self:WorldMarker(index, unit)  /  self:WorldMarker(index, x, y, z)
  self:TimedWorldMarker(duration, index, ...)
  self:ClearWorldMarker(index), self:ClearWorldMarkers()
  self:CanPlaceWorldMarkers()

The DLL syncs markers to the group, so only one client places them:
the raid leader by default ("assist" option lets any leader/assist
place). Requires the DLL and leader/assist permission; silently does
nothing otherwise. Markers placed by a module are cleared when the
fight ends (option). Includes a Test button under Plugins > World
Markers. No boss module uses it yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WJLQrM2ob1poW3peUyML4T
